00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,220
Listen to a talk in a biology class.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,891
Man:

3
00:00:04,891 --> 00:00:09,140
The phenomenon of animal migration is a fascinating subject in biology.

4
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:14,644
Migration involves the regular, often seasonal movement of animals from one region to another,

5
00:00:14,644 --> 00:00:18,280
typically in search of food, breeding grounds, or better climates.

6
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:25,160
This behavior is observed in a wide variety of species, including birds, mammals, fish, and insects.

7
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:29,230
One of the most well known examples is the migration of monarch butterflies.

8
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:36,120
These butterflies travel thousands of miles from North America to central Mexico to escape the cold winter.

9
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:41,120
This journey involves multiple generations, as no single butterfly makes the round trip.

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:45,060
Another remarkable example is the migration of humpback whales.

11
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:52,180
These massive creatures travel from their feeding grounds in polar waters to warmer tropical regions where they breed and give birth.

12
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:59,387
Birds like the Arctic tern undertake one of the longest migrations, traveling from the Arctic to the Antarctic

13
00:00:59,387 --> 00:01:00,290
and back each year.

14
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:09,010
Despite their differences in size, species and reasons for migrating, they all migrate vast distances with precision.

15
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:16,210
They navigate like seasoned human pilots flying transcontinental routes, only without aircraft, instruments or GPS.

16
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:19,250
Of course, migration is not without its challenges.

17
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:27,290
Animals must navigate vast distances, often facing predators, adverse weather and human made obstacles like buildings and roads.

18
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:35,110
Protecting habitats and reducing human interference can help maintain the delicate balance that allows migration to occur.

19
00:01:35,110 --> 00:01:43,120
Understanding animal migration provides insight into the complex behaviors and survival strategies of various species.
